WEBVTT

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:29.230
<i>The scientific civilization that Jean built up on the desert island</i>

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:36.110
<i>was ruined in one night by the rain, wind and waves of the typhoon.</i>

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:41.280
<i>In addition, the typhoon has brought a new island.</i>

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.450
<i>It is a wonder of Mother Nature.</i>

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.080
<i>While they were exploring the island,</i>

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.920
<i>they met Ayerton and the Kings of Terror there.</i>

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.630
There are the...

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.970
Kings of Terror!

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.930
A huge animal like that must be a monster from a previous age!

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.850
What will happen to us?

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:12.520
The world will be destroyed by the Kings of Terror in July, 1899.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.190
What's that?

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.490
A prophecy!

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:18.070
But we still have ten years left.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.910
Perhaps he will destroy everything gradually.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.160
You mean...

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.080
We are the first ones?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.370
Let's escape!

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:30.460
What?

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.590
Wait!

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.270
Wow! I can run really fast!

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:56.570
Not just running! Watch me!

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.200
Go!

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.450
What a convenient island!

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.870
Here we go!

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.730
Oh, no!

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.990
Stop me!

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.360
Make us stop!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.120
Leave it to me!

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.240
Oh, are they your servants?

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.330
Shut up! Kill me if you want!

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:58.880
How stupid! You ran around the island so fast you came right back!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:04.680
My private fleet will find this island soon! You'll be sorry then!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.430
I'm sick and tired of your boasts!

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.470
Just give up!

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.060
Okay! I got you! Let's make a deal!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.980
I promise you won't regret it!

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.730
Shut up!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.200
I have good news! Just listen!

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:31.950
Stop us!

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.010
Ouch! I stopped!

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:51.970
Careless of anyone else's problems, the Grandis Gang is here!

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.980
Ms. Grandis?

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.900
Is it really Nadia?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.400
Jean!

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.980
Marie! King!

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.820
You're alive!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.580
I see, the Nautilus was sunk.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:19.040
Captain Nemo is the person who helped us escape.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.960
I can't believe that submarine was beaten.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.630
Gargoyle's space battleship was stronger after all.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.010
So my dear Nemo was...

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.930
Electra too.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.220
All of them were killed.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.280
My dearest Nemo...

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.820
Such a big ship!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.830
Yeah, really big!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:57.670
I can't believe such a huge submarine has been built already.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:01.420
What a bunch of heartless people!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.380
Welcome to our ship. Nice to have you on board.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.010
Sanson, you don't have to identify yourself to a girl wearing a mask!

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.930
You are right. I must apologize. I am Electra.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:13.680
May I come in?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:16.100
What do you want?

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.350
I'm the captain of this ship. My name is Nemo.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.820
May I have your name again?

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.690
It's Nemo. Good day.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:27.900
Nemo... Captain Nemo...

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.080
I'll never see him again.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.830
Don't worry.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:40.080
I'm sure they are alive somewhere.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.500
You've become strong while we were away, Jean. Right, Nadia?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.090
I wonder.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:49.510
You don't have an eye for men.

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.510
I'm glad you're safe.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.720
We owe it to my Gratan.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.520
But what are you doing on this island?

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:02.190
Thank you for asking me about that. It's a long and epic story.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.190
We'd left the Nautilus to make a counterattack

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.530
when it was cornered by Gargoyle's space battleship.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:15.030
I remember! You flew away after that.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:20.290
Oh, no! We had a chance to counterattack during the battle.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:26.050
I, Sanson, gave the greatest blow to the space battleship.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.260
Everything was good so far.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.600
A hole was made in the Gratan after that,

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.180
and we were blown off into the distant sky.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:42.020
And then, after many days, we drifted ashore on this island.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:47.320
And we found this fool of a count already here.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.900
What? What do you mean, fool?

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:54.070
Don't you ever, ever call me that!

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:59.370
Shut up, you fool! If you're a fool, I'll call you a fool. You fool!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:03.460
You jerk! Didn't I just tell you not to call me a fool!

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.840
I'll call you a fool if I feel like it!

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.880
Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool!

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:17.050
So, the witch was you all along?

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.850
Witch?

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:21.310
That's what he told us.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.690
He's just a big liar!

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:26.480
You'd better be careful too.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.070
A big liar?

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.690
He thinks he's better than anyone else.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:35.780
He stole our liquor, and drank it all.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.580
That was why he was buried in the sand.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:42.250
I thought it was strange. We shouldn't have believed him so readily.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:46.460
So, the Gratan landed here because the balloon was holed?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.670
That's why we can't get off this island.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:52.470
Why don't you just mend the balloon?

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:55.930
That's true. I suppose we could do it with this many people.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.640
It's been a long time since I had a taste of something scientific!

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.600
You sound pretty sentimental.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.060
We've been stuck on that desert island.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.690
This island is also deserted.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:10.940
Science is something that starts from nothing.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.030
You're right.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.990
But it seems this island is not an ordinary desert island.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:23.660
There are no other humans here, but something seems to be alive.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.670
You mean there's something strange here after all?

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:29.250
Ayerton is not altogether a liar.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.250
That's right!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.220
I'm not a liar, or a boaster, either. Much less a fool!

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.550
What are you then?

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.140
I'm the true Count Ayerton!

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:45.480
Farewell, everybody!

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:47.770
What's that?

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.520
Goodbye!

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:53.190
He's gone.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.690
Where in the world is he going?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.660
He intends to escape on my boat!

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.320
What?

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.740
He's going to our island!

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:07.330
Is there another island near here?

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.010
What happened?

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.180
The island is getting smaller.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:21.760
Smaller?

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:28.850
What's that? There's really an island?

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.810
Did you all come from that island?

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.730
Yeah.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:36.030
Strange, there wasn't any island there before.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.700
That's right, Hanson.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.070
This island appeared suddenly last night.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.370
Impossible!

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:46.200
This island suddenly appeared last night,

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.660
and that one became smaller tonight!

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:49.170
That's it!

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.210
The island is moving!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:55.380
Oh, boy! Even you talk that way, Jean? But that can't be true.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:57.840
That's the only answer.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:01.050
It can't really happen.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.220
Hanson!

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:02.970
What?

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.600
What is most important for a scientist?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.060
What's that?

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.100
A sixth sense.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.060
A sixth sense?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:14.730
There are lots of things on Earth that humans don't understand yet.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:18.030
It's the duty of scientists to make them clear.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:19.490
I see.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.280
The sun also rises tomorrow.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:26.450
My theory will be scientifically proven.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.660
We must get back to that island for me to do so.

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.210
Why?

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:35.000
I left all of the encyclopedias over there!

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.220
It's really gone a long way.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.100
Maybe it's really moving.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.060
It will go farther away tomorrow.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.770
We'll move to Sanson's island, right?

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:55.230
Is it all right with you if we move to the strange island?

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:58.690
Sure! Marie likes that island because everybody is there!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:03.610
That's true. It's much more secure than living all alone by ourselves.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.410
I guess so. Our hut was destroyed anyway.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:11.330
If that island is moving as you've said,

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.380
someday, I might be able to go to my homeland.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:41.190
Wash the dishes quickly and help me with this.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:46.030
But there are so many to wash, it's going to take some time.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:48.870
You know we must cook a special dish for you.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:50.950
So keep working quickly!

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.580
You don't have to!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:57.170
I haven't asked you to do anything for me.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.840
You're stubborn as always.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:04.260
You'll lose Jean's love if you stay like that.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.180
Let's eat!

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.890
Wow! It looks delicious!

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:17.600
Are you really happy with this? What have you been eating until now?

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:21.400
We eat this every day. I'm tired of it.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.320
It's as hot as ever!

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:30.030
Don't eat it if you don't like it. Right, Nadia?

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.910
Why are you wearing a mask?

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.620
She doesn't like the smell of fish.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:41.460
Poor girl, she doesn't like it?

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.260
Thanks for the food!

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.880
Now, shall we make a hut?

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:47.550
A hut?

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.220
The present hut is too small.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.720
So, we'll make a new one!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.640
Hey, Hanson! Jean will be with me!

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:58.440
Darn! I thought he was going to help fix the Gratan's operational system.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:04.530
Hanson, today is your turn to wash dishes! Do your work after washing.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:06.990
Say, Ms. Grandis...

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.490
What is it?

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.700
Please allow me to cook lunch.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.490
I want to try.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.750
But can you do it?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.460
I don't know.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:22.130
Try it, then. There's always a first time for everything.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.420
If you cook, I could spend time by myself.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:28.970
Hey, Jean...

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:29.840
What?

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.810
Are you getting along well with Nadia?

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.770
Yeah, we're doing okay.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.810
So, have you done it?

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:40.230
Done it? What do you mean?

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:43.610
What? Well, it's just...

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.150
Oh, no, Sanson!

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:51.120
It's just that, if you love each other, it's a natural thing to do.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.950
But we don't have a chance as we're always quarreling.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.660
Okay! I'll give you some good advice.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:03.340
Listen up! Women become weak at the sight of a man's body.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:05.800
They're attracted by our strong muscles.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:09.760
I'm sure Nadia likes that kind of man.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:13.260
I see! I have to take up sports to build up my body!

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.390
Use this to exercise with.

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:21.100
Girls used to make fun of me too. They called me a feeble baby.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:24.570
So I worked desperately to build myself up.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:29.990
Nobody despised me after I became a strong, muscular man!

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:36.080
So, Jean. You can't capture a girl's heart with inventions.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.580
How is this?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:42.120
Oh, right there, yes, right there! That feels so good!

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.330
Is lunch ready yet?

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:48.550
Not yet. We'll have Nadia's special lunch today.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:51.010
Is Nadia cooking?

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:55.720
Hey! You'd better make it hotter if you want it to be good.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.890
How do I check it for taste?

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:08.860
What are you doing?

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:13.320
I'm in training to build up my muscles.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:18.040
You want to attract Nadia's attention that way, right?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.000
I can see that.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.210
You can?

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:28.130
Don't worry. Nadia is doing her best to cook a yummy meal for you.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:29.920
Right?

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.920
She is?

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.470
What is this?

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.930
A meal.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.930
As nice as one of Grandis' meals...

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:47.400
This is Nadia's first try at cooking. Let's try it!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:49.530
Delicious.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:52.190
But the plates are kind of dirty.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:55.660
That's your fault! Nadia had to wash the dishes herself!

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:59.370
But I had to fix the Gratan.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.410
It's delicious, Nadia!

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.370
Really?

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:04.790
It may not look so good, but...

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:09.040
What's wrong?

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:13.760
Jean!

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:19.560
Oh, boy...

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.140
I'm sorry, Jean.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.100
Don't trouble yourself over this.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:28.940
Men don't give up on those they love so easily.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:32.570
Will he forgive me?

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.070
Don't worry. It'll be okay.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.370
Don't worry. It'll really be okay.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:43.330
You said I shouldn't forgive Nadia, but I don't know what to do.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.250
You shouldn't do anything at a time like this.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.670
Do nothing?

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:51.340
That's right. Don't talk to her until she apologizes.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.760
Oh, no. I can't ignore her!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:59.470
Listen, Jean. Scientists should never make any mistakes.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.100
Girls will take advantage of your kindness.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.720
Are you sure?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:08.350
Look at me. I was too kind to Grandis, and now look at me.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:09.770
I don't know.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:14.320
Anyway, women like men who know a lot.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:20.620
They love men who can show off their intelligence. Nadia is the same.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:24.750
I see! I should study and invent more!

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:28.670
But Sanson said I should be more athletic.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:34.210
You can't catch a girl's heart just by being athletic like Sanson!

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.630
Okay! I'll study!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:40.800
I'll catch Nadia's heart by studying and inventing!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:47.230
I got it! The sun appears to move slowly, because the island is going east.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.390
Hey, Jean, are you studying again?

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:53.110
No, Sanson, I'm calculating the location of this island.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:56.110
Calculating? That's the same as studying.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:19:02.070
Forget it. You should train, or you will be ugly like Hanson.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:06.700
But he told me my brain will turn to muscle if I work out too much.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.540
What?

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.170
No! Never!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:18.880
Listen, Jean! Women seek in men what they don't have themselves.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:22.180
And men do the same in their search for women.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:25.600
Do you know what men have that women don't?

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:26.560
A moustache?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:28.520
No! Power!

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:29.480
Power?

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:33.860
Men protect their women with their power and muscles! And women...

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:34.820
Women?

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:35.770
Cook!

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:43.070
We won't live long if we keep eating like this.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:47.160
You shouldn't have let Nadia cook our meal again!

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:49.660
It's not that I'm being lazy.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:53.790
She asked me to let her do it!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:57.300
Why didn't you stop her? This is the second time!

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:02.220
It's only happened twice! She'll be better at cooking soon!

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:08.220
Hopeful young men may go to Heaven before her cooking gets any better.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:11.980
But the Seniorita's cooking isn't that different from Nadia's.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:16.860
What was that? When did I make something that killed people?

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:21.570
Hold on there! Nadia didn't mean to do anything bad. Let's forgive her.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:25.530
You're saying it doesn't matter if you don't mean to?

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:28.540
Don't jump to conclusions!

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:32.540
That's right! Hot food tastes better.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:37.960
I wish I could leave this island and eat better food!

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:40.460
Hanson, why don't you hurry up and fix the Gratan already?

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:44.010
Because you keep using Jean!

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:47.390
Oh, that's enough, everybody.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:51.850
It's silly of you to fight about such a trifling thing.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:53.810
Jean...

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:59.780
Right, you must think of the welfare of others first when in a group.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:04.610
Then, happiness will be sure to follow on its own.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:10.580
Oh, you speak like a real count.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:12.580
Ah, that reminds me...

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.870
I miss those days in England.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:21.130
My pockets were always filled with gold!

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:24.970
I invited lots of girls on my birthday,

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:28.300
and had a party that lasted three days.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:30.100
There was liquor from all over the world,

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:37.310
and extravagant meals of all kinds spread on the table!

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:52.200
He's a good boy.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:53.290
Who?

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:58.210
There aren't many boys who would cover up for someone else's failure.

00:21:58.210 --> 00:21:59.960
But...

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:03.920
You're afraid he might lose interest in you.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:09.930
It can't be helped. Women are always like that.

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:10.640
Really?

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:13.850
Women in love, I mean.

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:17.140
Jealousy, attachment, anxiety...

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:22.570
Those complicated feelings fill our heads.

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:25.610
Other things become meaningless.

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:30.280
That's love.

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:35.870
I've never been in love before.

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:38.330
The truth is, I didn't want to love anybody.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:42.960
But I never imagined it would be anything like this.

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:44.420
You mean about Jean?

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:50.760
I didn't know that loving someone meant I would feel so much pain.

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:56.680
That's true. I've cried so many times over it myself.

00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:58.270
Really?

00:22:58.270 --> 00:23:00.440
I remember each time.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:03.980
Every time I was a woman in love.

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:06.230
Say, Nadia...

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:07.190
What?

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:10.860
Was Captain Nemo your father after all?

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:16.620
I'm sorry! I shouldn't have asked you that.

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:19.580
It's okay. It's true.

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:22.500
Oh, how painful...

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:26.420
But you still have Sanson and Hanson!

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.380
They're like the moon.

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:36.470
They go around and around me, but they never try to get any closer.

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:40.890
Oh, yes!

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:41.900
What is it?

00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:44.980
You can call me Mama from now on.

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:46.320
Mama?

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:49.780
Because Captain Nemo is your father.

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:51.950
Mama...
